  "notes": "Modified cash basis county (governmental funds only); Total Governmental Funds column on p5 (Exhibit III, right half of the statement, p4 left half) used. The statement is split across p4-5 (receipts/disbursements) and p6-7 (balances); beginning cash 2,852,287 and ending 2,553,039 from p7. Transfers from/to other funds 860,000 each. 'Intergovernmental Receipts' 1,814,667 split into federal 329,074 and state 1,485,593 from the Federal/State lines of Schedules 1-2 (ties exactly). 'Local Fees, Licenses, Commissions, and Miscellaneous' (1,858,489): Inheritance Tax Fund column 133,406 split out as inheritance tax and Ambulance/Reg Deeds local 20,931 as charges; the rest (mostly Bridge local 1,518,973) has no breakdown, so other with review. 'Debt Service' 395,630 is combined principal and interest (bridge fund). Detail recorded: Schedule 1 General Fund (department/object; this is the same fund as the statement's General Fund column, no double counting) and Schedule 2 Special Revenue Funds (recorded under fund 'Special Revenue Funds' with the fund name in department because Schedule 2 prints only one overall total). Schedule 1 total disbursements 2,421,588 includes the 860,000 transfer (miscellaneous department), recorded as other financing -860,000 with includes. Schedule 2 total receipts 4,053,546 includes bridge transfers 860,000 (other financing). Zero-actual lines (drug law enforcement, veteran's aid operating, inheritance tax transfers, etc.) and lines with blank actuals omitted. Schedule 3 (fund balance rollforward) and Schedule 4 (combined statement) are duplicates of the statements and are not recorded as detail. Generic 'Operating' object lines have no matching object category and are marked miscellaneous expenditure with review. Statement p5 function totals differ slightly from schedule groupings (e.g. general government 1,110,026 vs 1,117,858 in Schedule 1 excluding transfers) because of classification differences. Read pages 1-19 of 19."
